WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.957 line:88% align:center
Keep Codex App open, then select Start gateway in Mobile Bridge.

2
00:00:05.957 --> 00:00:11.425 line:88% align:center
Expand QR sign-in and scan with your phone. Another computer can
open the address directly.

3
00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:15.505 line:88% align:center
The gateway has its own login; model authentication stays in Codex
App. This demo code cannot sign you in.

4
00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:22.382 line:88% align:center
Find local and SSH chats in one browser. Select a chat to continue
your work.

5
00:00:22.382 --> 00:00:30.020 line:88% align:center
Send a follow-up in the same chat. This example keeps its custom
model and reasoning effort.

6
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:36.720 line:88% align:center
Use Reminders to follow the chat and optionally enable completion
notifications.

7
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.828 line:88% align:center
Next-release preview: attach multiple files or images using the
paperclip control.

8
00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:49.916 line:88% align:center
Review the attachments and message, then send. You can remove files
or queue them with a task.

9
00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:57.226 line:88% align:center
Next-release preview: Plan mode leaves a plan in the chat for you to
review.

10
00:00:57.226 --> 00:01:03.084 line:88% align:center
Request changes if needed, or select Implement plan to continue with
the agreed work.

11
00:01:03.084 --> 00:01:08.016 line:88% align:center
Next-release preview: expand an active goal to see its objective and
token usage.

12
00:01:08.016 --> 00:01:11.165 line:88% align:center
Hide the goal panel to give the conversation more room. The goal
keeps running.

13
00:01:11.165 --> 00:01:14.769 line:88% align:center
Select Goal progress beside Send to bring the panel back.

14
00:01:14.769 --> 00:01:17.984 line:88% align:center
Collapse the composer while reading. Display settings control
process details, theme and text size.

15
00:01:17.984 --> 00:01:21.830 line:88% align:center
Open the model panel to view the full name and reasoning effort.
This example uses official login.

16
00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.403 line:88% align:center
Next-release preview: Fast appears when the account, model and
workspace allow it.

17
00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:31.751 line:88% align:center
Saved settings apply from the next turn. Fast uses more allowance;
turning it off restores standard speed.

18
00:01:31.751 --> 00:01:34.761 line:88% align:center
Next-release preview: green dots show running work across multiple
chats.

19
00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:41.627 line:88% align:center
A blue unread indicator remains after completion and clears when you
open the chat.

20
00:01:41.627 --> 00:01:46.755 line:88% align:center
The same web interface adapts to a computer display, showing the
chat list and conversation side by side.

21
00:01:46.755 --> 00:01:58.125 line:88% align:center
Choose your theme, language, text size and process details.
Preferences stay in this browser.

22
00:01:58.125 --> 00:02:01.627 line:88% align:center
Next-release preview: review watched chats and their execution hosts
on the desktop.

23
00:02:01.627 --> 00:02:08.666 line:88% align:center
Toggle completion notifications or remove a watch you no longer
need. The chat itself is retained.
